# Cursor Rules

## Cursor Behavior
- Cursor should be visible at all times during text editing
- Cursor should blink at a rate of 500ms on, 500ms off
- Cursor color should contrast with background for visibility
- Cursor width should be 2px for normal mode, 1px for insert mode

## Navigation Rules
- Arrow keys move cursor in corresponding directions
- Home/End keys move to beginning/end of line
- Page Up/Down keys move viewport by one page
- Ctrl+Left/Right moves cursor by word
- Ctrl+Home/End moves to beginning/end of document

## Selection Rules
- Shift+Arrow keys extend selection in direction of arrow
- Shift+Home/End extends selection to beginning/end of line
- Ctrl+A selects entire document
- Double-click selects word
- Triple-click selects paragraph

## Multi-cursor Support
- Alt+Click creates additional cursor
- Ctrl+Alt+Up/Down creates cursors on adjacent lines
- Escape key returns to single cursor mode

## Accessibility
- Cursor should be configurable for high-contrast mode
- Cursor size should be adjustable for visibility needs
- Cursor blink rate should be configurable, including option to disable blinking
